ANACREON 13
"PTM - Op:Holy War"
0     ; random scenario
2 8  ; 2-8 players
85    ; 85 by 85 galaxy
200   ; 200 planets
2     ; Difficulty: Advanced
100 0 ; 100+ years
4386

BEGINTEXT

This scenario was initially used to track the progress of the eight
primary empires in a novel I've been working on. It is perhapse the
most complex scenario ever written, and easily the strangest.

The map size for this scenario is signifigantly larger than any map
I've seen used before. Each of the empires fit the mold of an empire
in the story, so it's not as balanced as any other scenarios would
try to be.

NEWPAGE

Everything by the book;

Empire one, The Midnight Fellowship, is a reclusive empire more
concerned with maintaining their own borders than actual conquest.
The Fellowship is located in the top central portion of the Corallus
galaxy, and has the best defensive position of the standard empires.
Their world count is medium.

Empire two, Quelani imperium, is a production based empire with
more emphasis on attacking than defending. They are located within
the left most regions of the Corallus galaxy. Their world count is
medium - low.

The third and forth empires were once part of a single alliance,
but a difference of opinion within their heirchy resulted in their
planetary holdings being split down the center. Each of these empires
has a large world count.

NEWPAGE

Empire three is the Information society, inhabiting the right and
central sections of the corallus star system.

Empire four is the Secret Society, inhabiting the lower left and
central sections of the corallus star system.

Empire five, the nameless aliance, is the newest of the empires.
it was created to stop the war between the secret society and
information society. their world count is very low, but they have
more 'general fleets'. A general that defected from the Midnight
Fellowship has also offered to join their cause - if he can
survive the journey to the furthest southen section of the corallus
galaxy.

NEWPAGE

The Corallus galaxy is the dense area of stars on the top left
segment of the map. The planetary system at the bottom right is
the new home of the Elderos empire, which left Corallus 2000 years
ago, but they plan on returning. They are the sixth empire, and
have the most "general fleets". It will take a lot of time for
them to reach corallus. If the current leaders of Corallus don't
settle their differences quickly, Elderos' return could be death
for all of them.

The seventh empire is Klaetharia, which has many generals, but
no worlds of their own. This Hive like species is bent on rebuilding
their once great empire. They start off in the top right section of
the Corallus galaxy.

NEWPAGE

The last empire, number eight, is The Daerani Federation, which
is a small peaceful empire in the bottom right of the corallus
system Their world count is low, and they are less technically
advanced than the other empires. They aren't much of a threat
to the other empires, and will be ignored if they're lucky.

Inceasing turn times is Reccomended.

ENDTEXT
